; ── Browser (js_of_ocaml) build of the Tesl compiler ──────────────────────────
;
; This target is DELIBERATELY invisible to plain `dune build` — and therefore to
; ci.sh, the nix derivation and every developer without js_of_ocaml installed.
; It is gated on the release profile; see the long note on the stanza below for
; why that mechanism and not another.  Build it explicitly:
;
;     dune build --profile release playground/tesl_playground_js.bc.js
;
; or, from the repo root, `playground/build.sh`.
;
; Requires js_of_ocaml (library) and js_of_ocaml-compiler (the `js_of_ocaml`
; binary) on PATH; both are in the nix dev shell.

(executable
 (name tesl_playground_js)
 (modules tesl_playground_js)
 ; -warn-error +8 to match the compiler library's fail-closed discipline.
 (flags (:standard -warn-error +8))
 (modes js)
 ; ── Why this stanza is gated on the RELEASE profile ──────────────────────────
 ; An empty `(alias (name default))` override does NOT work, and that was the
 ; first attempt: "Library js_of_ocaml not found" is raised while dune RESOLVES
 ; the rule, before any alias gets to decide whether to build it.  So plain
 ; `dune build` — and therefore ci.sh phase 1 — failed on every machine without
 ; js_of_ocaml, which is precisely what the exclusion exists to prevent.
 ;
 ; `%{env:...}` would be the direct way to express "opt in", but it needs
 ; (lang dune 3.15) and this project is on 3.0; bumping the language version to
 ; gate one optional target would change defaults across the whole build.
 ;
 ; `%{profile}` needs no version bump.  Everything that must keep working on a
 ; machine without js_of_ocaml uses the DEV profile — plain `dune build`,
 ; `dune test`, ci.sh, and flake.nix's `dune build bin/main.exe` — so gating on
 ; release disables the stanza for all of them, while `playground/build.sh`
 ; (which already passes --profile release) still builds it.
 ;
 ; The cost, stated: `dune build --profile release` now requires js_of_ocaml.
 ; Nothing in the repo does that today.
 (enabled_if (= %{profile} release))
 (libraries tesl_compiler_lib js_of_ocaml))
